  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Oxidation number of of copper is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>Due to the absence of unpaired electrons, their spin only magnetic moment is zero, they are diamagnetic in nature</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;one unpaired electron is present.Hence, paramagnetic in nature.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>one</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>unpaired</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electron</mi></math>.Hence, paramagnetic in nature.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>"
